A new window leaves every share charged with what it spent in the last.
A share that spent its budget never has it again;
no share was charged more ticks than the window has had.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: share was charged more ticks than the window has had

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -239,7 +239,6 @@ void sched_window_start(void)
     window_ticks = window_idle = 0;
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < SHARES; i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(SHARES);
-        shares[i].used = 0;
         share_settle(&shares[i]);
     }
 }
